# Commit & push authorship

Every commit must be attributed to the **human developer who authored the
change**, using that developer's own configured git identity. Never attribute a
commit to Cursor or any other AI agent.

## Rules

- The commit **author and committer** must be the real developer's name and
  email (whatever they have set in their local git config, e.g.
  `git config user.name` / `git config user.email`). Do **not** override or
  hard-code a specific person's identity.
- **Never** author or co-author a commit as an AI agent. In particular, do
  **not** add a `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` trailer (or
  any other AI/agent co-author trailer) to commit messages.
- Before any `git push`, verify the commits being pushed are authored by a real
  developer and contain no AI/agent attribution.

## How to enforce

Each developer sets their own identity once (do this per developer, not as a
shared value):

```bash
git config user.name  "Your Name"
git config user.email "you@tenstorrent.com"
```

If a commit is created with a stray `Co-authored-by: Cursor` trailer, strip it
before pushing:

```bash
# Last commit only:
git commit --amend --no-edit

# Strip the trailer from the last N unpushed commits (N = range vs origin/main):
FILTER_BRANCH_SQUELCH_WARNING=1 git filter-branch -f \
  --msg-filter 'sed "/^Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>$/d"' \
  origin/main..HEAD
```

Verify before pushing (author must be a real developer, never an AI agent):

```bash
git log origin/main..HEAD --format='%an <%ae> | %s'
```
